%description:

Tcp.mtuProbing:invalid -- the value 3 stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts 0, 1 and 2.

The classes: off (0, the default; 1 is the same, because INET has no detector of black holes),
search (2), invalid (below 0, above 2). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables()
checks the value; with 2, TcpConnection::initMtuProbing() starts an active opener at the base
MSS, and TcpConnection::sendData() sends a probe larger than the MSS when the window has 11
segments; the ACK of the probe raises the MSS.

Host under test: host1. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.mtuProbing
%# class: invalid
%# value: 3
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mtuProbing
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpMtuProbingInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mtuProbing = 3    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
mtuProbing must be 0, 1 or 2, but it is 3
